      "Chapter conclusion: Dependence can serve two different purposes: seeking positive emotions through dopamine, or suppressing pain, depression, anxiety and chronic stress. Brief, moderate stress adds vitality and motivation, whereas chronic stress disrupts reward systems and increases vulnerability to destructive dependence."
